+
+### Launchpad host firewall admission
+
+Dedicated Launchpad nodes enable `LAUNCHPAD_REQUIRE_HOST_FIREWALL`. Immediately
+before Create starts a guest (including prepared activation), the host runs
+`/usr/local/libexec/launchpad-host-firewall check` with a bounded deadline.
+Missing installation or rules changed since the systemd service applied them
+refuse new execution; existing admitted workloads continue. The root-owned
+service must apply the pinned guest firewall on each host boot before E2B
+starts. Its receipt records both policy bytes and active nftables rules, excluding
+only counters and kernel-assigned handles. Service-active alone is insufficient:
+a later ruleset flush must make admission fail. Ordinary upstream nodes retain
+the default-off setting. This guard is independent of API team admission and
+does not make external management ports safe to expose publicly.
